XLSX formulas keep Excel's bare TRUE and FALSE

Excel writes a logical constant in a formula as TRUE or FALSE. Calc
parses the bare word as the function TRUE() or FALSE(), adding the
parentheses, and wrote them back, so every save changed the formula
text Excel shows (Ely R15.11f). The OOXML writer now drops the empty
parentheses after TRUE and FALSE; the value is the same in Excel and
Calc. A file that spelled FALSE() itself is also written FALSE.
